#: {{ux|en|Rain tomorrow is '''possible''', but I wouldn't bet on it.}}
#: {{ux|en|It's not just '''possible''', it's probable that there will be rain tomorrow.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=8|passage=The humor of my proposition appealed more strongly to Miss Trevor than I had looked for, and from that time forward she became her old self again;{{...}}. Now she had come to look upon the matter in its true proportions, and her anticipation of a '''possible''' chance of teaching him a lesson was a pleasure to behold.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1978|last=Kołakowski|first=Leszek|authorlink=Leszek Kołakowski|title=w:Main Currents of Marxism|volume=I: The Founders|origlang=pl|original=Główne nurty marksizmu: powstanie|translator=P[aul] S[teven] Falla|origyear=1976|publisher=w:Clarendon Press|location=w:Oxford|isbn=9780198245476|oclc=181789472|page=418|passage=In short, the Leninist-Stalinist version of socialism was a '''possible''' interpretation, though certainly not the only '''possible''' one, of Marx's doctrine.}}
# {{lb|en|comparable}} Capable of being done or achieved; [[feasible]].
#: {{syn|en|achievable|doable|viable}}
#: {{ant|en|impossible}}
#: {{ux|en|It's '''possible''' for anyone to learn to play the bagpipes.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1901|author=Louis Freeland Smith|title=The Public|volume=4|page=438|pageurl=http://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=inu.30000080738168&page=search;seq=444;view=image;num=438
|passage=And success in minor degree, in the sense in which he uses the term "success," is only somewhat more '''possible''' than success in winning the White House chair.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=1993 September 10|author=Lee Michael Katz|title=Expectant Mideast hopes to bear twin peace deals|journal=USA Today|page=2A|url=http://pqasb.pqarchiver.com/USAToday/access/55212520.html?dids=55212520:55212520&FMT=ABS&FMTS=ABS:FT|passage=Peace between Israel and the Arab countries is "more '''possible''' than any time before," says ex-Arab League U.N. ambassador Clovis Maskoud.|accessdate=25 August 2009|archiveurl=https://archive.today/20130630061707/http://pqasb.pqarchiver.com/USAToday/access/55212520.html?dids=55212520:55212520&FMT=ABS&FMTS=ABS:FT|archivedate=30 June 2013}}
#* {{RQ:Economist|date=2013-06-29|volume=407|issue=8842|page=72–3
|title=A punch in the gut
|url=http://www.economist.com/news/international/science-and-technology/21580133-how-microbes-promote-liver-cancer-overweight-punch-gut
|passage=Mostly, the microbiome is beneficial. It helps with digestion and enables people to extract a lot more calories from their food than would otherwise be '''possible'''. Research over the past few years, however, has implicated it in diseases from atherosclerosis to asthma to autism.}}
# Being [[considered]], e.g. for a [[position]].
#: {{ux|en|Jones and Smith are both '''possible''' for the opening in sales.}}
# Apparently valid, likely, [[plausible]].
#: {{syn|en|likely|plausible}}
#: {{ant|en|implausible}}

